# =============================================================================
# syntax-hybrid.sem  —  hello-world webserver
#                       with arrays, records, and library iteration
# =============================================================================
# Hello-world HTTP server in the refined dialect. Iteration is a library
# call (array.reduce, array.forEachWithContext) invoked through the normal
# call lifecycle; the previous draft's forEach/endForEach primitive was
# dropped because it both nested SemanticScript inside SemanticScript and
# required cosmetic indentation that the spec says is non-semantic.
#
#   GET /         200 HTML  -> handleGreetingRequest
#   GET /healthz  200 JSON  -> handleHealthRequest
#   anything else 404 text  -> handleNotFoundRequest  (router default)
#
# Read alongside:
#   syntax-baseline.sem    the production dialect, as a control
#   syntax-refinement.sem  the maximalist proposal, as the starting point
#
# =============================================================================
# Constructs in use
# =============================================================================
#
# RECORD TYPES
#   record <RecordType>
#   field  <RecordType> <fieldName> <FieldType>
#   purpose / invariant lines attach to the record type the same way they
#   attach to operations and modules.
#
# RECORD VALUES  (constructed via the storage form with a record-typed axis)
#   storage <name>
#   scope / mutability / type as usual
#   fieldValue <name> <fieldName> <FieldType> <Value>     one per field
#
# ARRAY TYPES
#   type <Alias> arrayContaining <ElementType>      English unary constructor
#
# ARRAY VALUES  (constructed via the storage form with an array-typed axis)
#   storage <name>
#   scope / mutability / type as usual
#   initialElement <name> <Value>                          one per element,
#                                                          in declaration order
#
# FIELD AND ELEMENT ACCESS  (irreducible primitives — language-level shortcuts
# for record.field and array.element library calls)
#   fieldOf   <newBinding> <Type> <recordRef> <fieldName>
#   elementOf <newBinding> <Type> <arrayRef>  <indexValue>
#
# BRANCH AND BIND (baseline verbs kept; the structured branchOn / when
# experiment was rolled back because the baseline shape carries enough
# context and adds no fork burden)
#
#   label <name>                                    declare a destination
#   branch <target>                                 unconditional jump
#   branchIf <cond> <target>                        conditional jump on true;
#                                                   fall-through on false
#   branchIfError <call> <target>                   error-arm jump on a Result
#
#   bind <name> <Type> <call>                       bind a call's result
#   bindOk <name> <Type> <call>                     bind the ok arm of a Result
#   bindError <name> <Type> <call>                  bind the error arm
#
# Binary branching uses the baseline two-line pattern:
#
#   branchIf isGet returnIncremented                # jump on true
#   branch returnUnchanged                          # fall-through label
#
# Two lines, no closing sentinel, no per-line discriminant echo. The
# pattern is positional but every slot kind is distinct (cond is a
# camelCase value; target is a label name; `branch` always names its
# unconditional target). The earlier branchOn / when / endBranch
# experiment added context-loss on retrieved `when` lines (the
# discriminant lived offscreen on the opening branchOn) and forked
# the baseline grammar for no clear win — both reverted.
#
# ITERATION  (library calls, no primitive)
#   array.forEach(collection, step)                      side-effecting,
#                                                        no context
#   array.forEachWithContext(collection, step, context)  side-effecting,
#                                                        threads context
#                                                        to each step
#   array.reduce(collection, initialValue, step)         fold; accumulator
#                                                        threaded through
#   array.map(collection, step)                          new array, same
#                                                        length
#   array.filter(collection, predicate)                  new array, kept
#                                                        elements only
#   array.length(collection)                             element count
#   array.get(collection, index)                         element at index
#   array.new(elementType)                               empty mutable array
#   array.append(array, element)                         grow in place
#
# Each is a normal library function invoked through call -> argument* ->
# run -> bind. The step / predicate / handler is a typed Operation
# reference; the library threads the iteration state through it.
#
# LOCAL MUTABLE STATE  (full per-axis form)
#   storage <name>
#   scope <name> local
#   mutability <name> mutable
#   type <name> <Type>
#   initialValue <name> <Value>
#
#   set <slotName> <newValue>
#
# Why iteration is library, not primitive:
#   The previous draft used `forEach <iter> <Type> in <coll>` with a body
#   that nested SemanticScript inside SemanticScript. That body required
#   cosmetic indentation to scan — and the spec says indentation carries
#   no semantic weight. Either the indentation is misleading (looks like
#   it nests but doesn't) or the language has reintroduced indentation
#   semantics it explicitly rejects. Both are bad. Moving iteration to
#   library calls eliminates the inner SS-in-SS scope entirely. The step
#   is a normal named operation with its own contract; the iteration site
#   is one ordinary call. The verb table shrinks (no forEach / endForEach)
#   and every iteration variant (forEach / reduce / map / filter / take)
#   shares the same call-lifecycle shape.
#
# Why content blocks (htmlContent / jsonContent) still survive, without
# closing sentinels:
#   They are typed literal blocks of foreign content (the agent's prior
#   on HTML/JSON is massive). The block opens on `htmlContent <name>`
#   or `jsonContent <name>` at column 0 and ends when a non-blank line
#   returns to column 0. Content lines are indented; that indentation
#   belongs to the embedded language and is preserved verbatim. The
#   SemanticScript surface itself has no indentation — every SS line
#   is at column 0 — so the column-0-returns rule cleanly separates
#   "still inside the foreign block" from "back to SemanticScript".
#   No endHtmlContent / endJsonContent sentinel is needed; the dedent
#   does the work.
#
# Why arrays and records use the storage form, not parallel declarations:
#   Storage is already the declaration verb with slot-axis verbs
#   (scope / mutability / type / initialValue). Records and arrays
#   extend the axis surface (fieldValue, initialElement) rather than
#   introducing parallel `record alice ofType User` / `array xs of T`
#   declaration verbs. One declaration mechanism for every named, typed
#   value in the module — primitive scalar, record, or array.
#
# Why fieldOf and elementOf are primitives instead of library calls:
#   Field access and indexed element access are frequent enough that
#   expressing them as 4-6 line call lifecycles is a real cost. The
#   library forms (record.field, array.element) still exist; `fieldOf`
#   and `elementOf` are language-level shortcuts. Same justification as
#   `bind` itself: too common to spell out.
#
# Why `because` stays mandatory on ignoreError of Result types:
#   Dropping the error arm of a Result is the easiest correctness bug
#   for an agent to introduce by accident — preserving the call's shape
#   while quietly discarding the failure path. A bare ignoreError on a
#   Result is a linter error; the mandatory because "..." clause is the
#   cheapest correct-by-construction guard the language can buy.
# =============================================================================


# R14: line-leading provenance verb.
frozen module app.hello_server
frozen purpose app.hello_server "Hello-world HTTP server using library iteration over a route table built from records and arrays."
frozen invariant app.hello_server "GET / serves greetingDocument; GET /healthz serves healthResponseJson; everything else routes to handleNotFoundRequest."


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Type aliases
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

type RequestHandleResult resultReturning HttpResponse failingWith HandlerError
type StartServerResult resultReturning ServerHandle failingWith StartError
type StopServerResult resultReturning StopStatus failingWith StopError

type HttpRouteList arrayContaining HttpRouteEntry


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Record types
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

record HttpRouteEntry
field HttpRouteEntry method HttpMethod
field HttpRouteEntry path HttpRoutePath
field HttpRouteEntry handler HttpHandler
purpose HttpRouteEntry "One row in the application's route table."
invariant HttpRouteEntry "path must begin with `/` and contain no query string."
invariant HttpRouteEntry "handler must be an operation accepting (HttpRequest, HttpSession) and returning RequestHandleResult."


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Imports
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

importDependency http standard.http
importDependency log standard.log
importDependency runtime standard.runtime
importDependency math standard.math
importDependency enum standard.enum
importDependency array standard.array


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Module storage
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

storage notFoundBody
scope notFoundBody module
mutability notFoundBody immutable
type notFoundBody PlainTextBody
initialValue notFoundBody plainText "Not found\n"

storage listenPort
scope listenPort module
mutability listenPort immutable
type listenPort TcpPort
initialValue listenPort 8080

storage rootPath
scope rootPath module
mutability rootPath immutable
type rootPath HttpRoutePath
initialValue rootPath urlPath "/"

storage healthPath
scope healthPath module
mutability healthPath immutable
type healthPath HttpRoutePath
initialValue healthPath urlPath "/healthz"

storage bootTimeoutSeconds
scope bootTimeoutSeconds module
mutability bootTimeoutSeconds immutable
type bootTimeoutSeconds CSignedInt32
initialValue bootTimeoutSeconds 5

storage stopTimeoutSeconds
scope stopTimeoutSeconds module
mutability stopTimeoutSeconds immutable
type stopTimeoutSeconds CSignedInt32
initialValue stopTimeoutSeconds 10


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Record values
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

storage greetingRoute
scope greetingRoute module
mutability greetingRoute immutable
type greetingRoute HttpRouteEntry
fieldValue greetingRoute method HttpMethod HttpMethod.Get
fieldValue greetingRoute path HttpRoutePath rootPath
fieldValue greetingRoute handler HttpHandler handleGreetingRequest

storage healthRoute
scope healthRoute module
mutability healthRoute immutable
type healthRoute HttpRouteEntry
fieldValue healthRoute method HttpMethod HttpMethod.Get
fieldValue healthRoute path HttpRoutePath healthPath
fieldValue healthRoute handler HttpHandler handleHealthRequest


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Array value
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

storage appRoutes
scope appRoutes module
mutability appRoutes immutable
type appRoutes HttpRouteList
initialElement appRoutes greetingRoute
initialElement appRoutes healthRoute


# =============================================================================
# greetingDocument  —  the HTML page served at GET /
# =============================================================================
# Content is indented; the block opens on `htmlContent <name>` and ends
# when a non-blank line returns to column 0. The content's own
# indentation is preserved verbatim and is for the embedded language,
# not for SemanticScript.

htmlContent greetingDocument
  <!DOCTYPE html>
  <html lang="en">
    <head>
      <meta charset="utf-8">
      <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
      <title>Hello — SemanticScript</title>
      <style>
        body.page { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 36rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; color: #222; }
        h1 { margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
        p  { color: #555; }
        a  { color: #0a58ca; }
      </style>
    </head>
    <body class="page">
      <h1>Hello, world!</h1>
      <p>Served by SemanticScript on TCP 8080.</p>
      <p><a href="/healthz">view health JSON</a></p>
    </body>
  </html>


# =============================================================================
# healthResponseJson  —  the JSON body served at GET /healthz
# =============================================================================
# Same termination rule: block ends when a non-blank line returns to
# column 0. JSON's own indentation is preserved.

jsonContent healthResponseJson
  {
    "status": "ok",
    "service": "hello_server",
    "listenPort": 8080,
    "checks": {
      "listener": "bound",
      "handler": "ready",
      "degraded": false
    },
    "tags": ["alive", "responsive"]
  }


# =============================================================================
# operation handleGreetingRequest
# =============================================================================

operation handleGreetingRequest
input handleGreetingRequest httpRequest HttpRequest
input handleGreetingRequest httpSession HttpSession
output handleGreetingRequest RequestHandleResult
effect handleGreetingRequest read http.request
effect handleGreetingRequest write http.response
authority handleGreetingRequest http.response write
memoryHeap handleGreetingRequest no
async handleGreetingRequest no
purpose handleGreetingRequest "Render greetingDocument as a 200 HTML response."
invariant handleGreetingRequest "Response body derives from immutable module-scope HTML."

call buildHtmlOkCall http.responseHtml
argument buildHtmlOkCall status HttpStatus HttpStatus.Ok
argument buildHtmlOkCall document HtmlDocument greetingDocument
run buildHtmlOkCall
bind htmlResponse HttpResponse buildHtmlOkCall
returnOk htmlResponse


# =============================================================================
# operation handleHealthRequest
# =============================================================================

operation handleHealthRequest
input handleHealthRequest httpRequest HttpRequest
input handleHealthRequest httpSession HttpSession
output handleHealthRequest RequestHandleResult
effect handleHealthRequest read http.request
effect handleHealthRequest write http.response
authority handleHealthRequest http.response write
memoryHeap handleHealthRequest no
async handleHealthRequest no
purpose handleHealthRequest "Render healthResponseJson as a 200 JSON response."
invariant handleHealthRequest "Response body derives from immutable module-scope JSON."

call buildJsonOkCall http.responseJson
argument buildJsonOkCall status HttpStatus HttpStatus.Ok
argument buildJsonOkCall body JsonValue healthResponseJson
run buildJsonOkCall
bind jsonResponse HttpResponse buildJsonOkCall
returnOk jsonResponse


# =============================================================================
# operation handleNotFoundRequest
# =============================================================================

operation handleNotFoundRequest
input handleNotFoundRequest httpRequest HttpRequest
input handleNotFoundRequest httpSession HttpSession
output handleNotFoundRequest RequestHandleResult
effect handleNotFoundRequest read http.request
effect handleNotFoundRequest write http.response
authority handleNotFoundRequest http.response write
memoryHeap handleNotFoundRequest no
async handleNotFoundRequest no
purpose handleNotFoundRequest "Return notFoundBody as a 404 plaintext response."
invariant handleNotFoundRequest "Response body is constant module storage; request data is not echoed."

call build404Call http.responsePlainText
argument build404Call status HttpStatus HttpStatus.NotFound
argument build404Call body PlainTextBody notFoundBody
run build404Call
bind notFoundResponse HttpResponse build404Call
returnOk notFoundResponse


# =============================================================================
# operation incrementIfGet  —  leaf step of countGetRoutes
# =============================================================================
# Per-element step for array.reduce. Branching uses baseline
# branchIf <cond> <onTrueLabel> / branch <onFalseLabel> — jump on true,
# fall through on false. Two lines, every slot kind distinct, no
# closing sentinel.

operation incrementIfGet
input incrementIfGet currentCount CSignedInt32
input incrementIfGet route HttpRouteEntry
output incrementIfGet CSignedInt32
effect incrementIfGet read memory.none
memoryHeap incrementIfGet no
async incrementIfGet no
purpose incrementIfGet "Return currentCount + 1 if route's method is GET, else currentCount unchanged."
invariant incrementIfGet "Result is currentCount or currentCount + 1; no other transformations."

fieldOf routeMethod HttpMethod route method

call methodEqCall enum.equalHttpMethod
argument methodEqCall left HttpMethod routeMethod
argument methodEqCall right HttpMethod HttpMethod.Get
run methodEqCall
bind isGet Bool methodEqCall

branchIf isGet returnIncremented
branch returnUnchanged

label returnIncremented
call addCall math.addCSignedInt32
argument addCall left CSignedInt32 currentCount
argument addCall right CSignedInt32 1
run addCall
bind nextCount CSignedInt32 addCall
returnValue nextCount

label returnUnchanged
returnValue currentCount


# =============================================================================
# operation countGetRoutes  —  nested algorithm over the route array
# =============================================================================
# Fold over routes via array.reduce. The accumulator (count) and the step
# (incrementIfGet) are typed; the reduce library threads them together.
# No local mutable state, no forEach body, no set — the fold IS the
# nested algorithm, expressed in one library call.

operation countGetRoutes
input countGetRoutes routes HttpRouteList
output countGetRoutes CSignedInt32
effect countGetRoutes read memory.none
memoryHeap countGetRoutes no
async countGetRoutes no
purpose countGetRoutes "Return the number of GET routes in the input list."
invariant countGetRoutes "Result is non-negative and at most the input list's length."

call reduceCall array.reduce
argument reduceCall collection HttpRouteList routes
argument reduceCall initialValue CSignedInt32 0
argument reduceCall step Operation incrementIfGet
run reduceCall
bind totalCount CSignedInt32 reduceCall

returnValue totalCount


# =============================================================================
# operation registerRouteEntry  —  leaf step of route registration
# =============================================================================
# Per-element handler for array.forEachWithContext. Receives one
# HttpRouteEntry plus the target HttpRouter as a threaded context, and
# adds the entry to the router.

operation registerRouteEntry
input registerRouteEntry route HttpRouteEntry
input registerRouteEntry targetRouter HttpRouter
output registerRouteEntry CSignedInt32
effect registerRouteEntry write http.router
authority registerRouteEntry http.router write
memoryHeap registerRouteEntry no
async registerRouteEntry no
purpose registerRouteEntry "Add one HttpRouteEntry to the given router; per-element handler for array.forEachWithContext over a route table."
invariant registerRouteEntry "Returns the router-add status; does not mutate the route entry."

call addCall http.routerAddEntry
argument addCall router HttpRouter targetRouter
argument addCall entry HttpRouteEntry route
run addCall
bind addStatus CSignedInt32 addCall
returnValue addStatus


# =============================================================================
# operation main
# =============================================================================

operation main
output main ExitCode
effect main allocate net.tcpListener
effect main bind net.tcpPort
effect main allocate http.router
effect main spawn runtime.taskGroup
effect main read os.signal
effect main read module.appRoutes
authority main net.tcpListener allocate
authority main net.tcpPort bind
authority main http.router allocate
authority main os.signal read
memoryHeap main yes
async main no
purpose main "Build a router from the appRoutes table via array.forEachWithContext, log the GET-route count, bind one HTTP listener, and dispatch requests until an OS shutdown signal arrives."
invariant main "Router lifetime is bounded by the listener; the listener lifetime is bounded by the enclosing task group."

call createRouterCall http.routerNew
run createRouterCall
bind appRouter HttpRouter createRouterCall

call registerAllRoutesCall array.forEachWithContext
argument registerAllRoutesCall collection HttpRouteList appRoutes
argument registerAllRoutesCall step Operation registerRouteEntry
argument registerAllRoutesCall context HttpRouter appRouter
run registerAllRoutesCall
ignoreValue registerAllRoutesCall CSignedInt32

call setDefaultHandlerCall http.routerSetDefault
argument setDefaultHandlerCall router HttpRouter appRouter
argument setDefaultHandlerCall handler HttpHandler handleNotFoundRequest
run setDefaultHandlerCall
ignoreValue setDefaultHandlerCall CSignedInt32

call countCall countGetRoutes
argument countCall routes HttpRouteList appRoutes
run countCall
bind getRouteCount CSignedInt32 countCall

call logCountCall log.info
argument logCountCall event LogEventKind LogEventKind.RoutesRegistered
argument logCountCall count CSignedInt32 getRouteCount
run logCountCall
ignoreValue logCountCall CSignedInt32

call bootServerCall http.serverStart
timeout bootServerCall bootTimeoutSeconds
cancelOn bootServerCall processShutdownToken
argument bootServerCall port TcpPort listenPort
argument bootServerCall router HttpRouter appRouter
argument bootServerCall logger StructuredLogger log.default
run bootServerCall
bindOk serverHandle ServerHandle bootServerCall
bindError startError StartError bootServerCall
branchIfError bootServerCall startFailed

call awaitShutdownCall runtime.awaitAnySignal
argument awaitShutdownCall signal OsSignal OsSignal.Interrupt
argument awaitShutdownCall signal OsSignal OsSignal.Terminate
run awaitShutdownCall
bind shutdownReason ShutdownReason awaitShutdownCall

call stopServerCall http.serverStop
timeout stopServerCall stopTimeoutSeconds
argument stopServerCall server ServerHandle serverHandle
argument stopServerCall reason ShutdownReason shutdownReason
run stopServerCall
bindOk stopStatus StopStatus stopServerCall
bindError stopError StopError stopServerCall
ignoreError stopServerCall because "Process is exiting; a failed graceful stop is logged elsewhere and does not change the exit code."

call logStopCall log.info
argument logStopCall event LogEventKind LogEventKind.ServerStopped
argument logStopCall status StopStatus stopStatus
run logStopCall
ignoreValue logStopCall CSignedInt32

returnValue ExitCode.Ok

label startFailed
call logFailureCall log.error
argument logFailureCall event LogEventKind LogEventKind.StartupFailed
argument logFailureCall detail StartError startError
run logFailureCall
ignoreValue logFailureCall CSignedInt32
returnValue ExitCode.StartupFailed


# =============================================================================
# What changed and why
# =============================================================================
#
# Iteration moved from primitive to library:
#   The `forEach <iter> <Type> in <coll>` / `endForEach` block was dropped.
#   It nested SemanticScript inside SemanticScript and asked for cosmetic
#   indentation that the spec explicitly says is non-semantic. The body
#   either looked nested (misleading) or read as a flat dump (ugly). Both
#   were the wrong answer. Library-call iteration eliminates the inner
#   scope entirely; the step is a normal named operation, the iteration
#   site is one call. countGetRoutes is now a single array.reduce; route
#   registration is one array.forEachWithContext over appRoutes with
#   registerRouteEntry as the per-element step.
#
# The branch family was reverted to baseline:
#   The structured branchOn / when / whenDefault experiment lost local
#   meaning on retrieved `when` lines (the discriminant lived on the
#   opening branchOn, offscreen on partial retrieval) and forked the
#   baseline grammar with no clear net win. Reverted to baseline:
#   `label X`, `branch X`, `branchIf cond X`, `branchIfError call X`.
#   Binary Bool case is two lines (`branchIf cond onTrue` then
#   `branch onFalse`); multi-way switching can be expressed as a chain
#   of branchIf-equality checks against literals, or — better — as a
#   library call like `enum.dispatch` taking a typed step Operation per
#   case (same library-call pattern as iteration).
#
# HTML and JSON content blocks keep their native indentation, drop the
# sentinel:
#   The block opens on `htmlContent <name>` / `jsonContent <name>` at
#   column 0; the content is indented; the block ends when a non-blank
#   line returns to column 0. No endHtmlContent / endJsonContent line.
#   Indentation inside the block is the embedded language's own (HTML's
#   own visual structure, JSON's pretty-print), preserved verbatim by
#   the parser and ignored by SemanticScript itself. Because every SS
#   line is at column 0, the column-0-returns rule cleanly partitions
#   "foreign content" from "back to SS" with no ambiguity.
#
# Nested-algorithm pattern survives, expressed differently:
#   The "leaf operation per element + composition at the call site"
#   shape stayed. What changed is that the composition site is now
#   array.reduce / array.forEachWithContext instead of an inline
#   forEach body. The leaf operations (incrementIfGet,
#   registerRouteEntry) are unchanged in spirit — they take one
#   element plus whatever threaded state the library passes, and
#   return a typed result. The pattern reads as a one-line fold or
#   forEach at the call site, with the per-step logic factored into
#   a named operation that an agent can review independently.
#
# What this draft does NOT introduce:
#   - A `var X T V` shortcut for local mutables. Per-axis storage
#     form everywhere, even for any future loop-local accumulators.
#   - Inline record or array literals. All values are named storage.
#   - A break / continue surface for iteration. Library reduce /
#     forEach run to completion; early termination factors into the
#     step returning a typed IterationControl variant that the
#     library honors, or a recursive operation. Out of scope here.
#   - Any cosmetic indentation inside SemanticScript source. Every
#     SS line is at column 0; the grammar is flat, the source looks
#     flat. Content blocks contain foreign content which carries
#     its own whitespace rules; those blocks are also flat-left in
#     this draft because their indentation was non-semantic too.
#
# What remains an open question:
#   - Indexed iteration. `array.forEach` and `array.reduce` pass only
#     the element (and accumulator, for reduce). An indexed variant
#     (`array.forEachIndexed`) would pass (index, element) — same
#     library shape, different signature on the step. Add when needed.
#   - Multi-collection iteration (zip). `array.zipReduce` /
#     `array.zipForEach` library calls take two collections and a step
#     of the right arity. Same shape, different argument list.
#   - Map / filter convenience. Pure-functional collection ops are
#     library functions taking a typed step or predicate. Same shape
#     as reduce; no new grammar.
